invariant: INV-13
file: tcp_nonblocking_frame.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: tcp_nonblocking_fail names the alert in ch_record_alert and no longer
  records it for ch_alert_sent, so the one call a caller reads across its
  sessions says no failure chose an alert in the handshake of a
  tcp-nonblocking session. bin/tcp_nonblocking_loop_test requires both calls
  to name decrypt_error after a wrong pin.

--- old
    r->t.alert_sent = r->alert;
--- new
